# .bootstrap/actions — arm a recorded memo to surface AT a repeat-prone action (project-bootstrap)
#
# WHY this file exists: a fix already documented in memory does no good if it is never in
# front of the actor at the moment the action runs. A deploy-author bug recurred ~7 times
# despite a memory documenting the exact fix, because the memo was never surfaced when the
# prod deploy ran. Arming an action here makes inject-action-memory.sh (PreToolUse on Bash)
# inject that memo as advisory context right before the matched action executes.
#
# This is OPT-IN: copy this file into your repo's `.bootstrap/` folder as `actions` (i.e.
# `.bootstrap/actions`; the legacy flat path `.bootstrap-actions` is still read). With no file,
# the injector is completely silent (non-adopting repos are never disturbed). It NEVER blocks
# and NEVER acks — it only injects context; reading and applying the fix stays your job (an
# ack token would be self-issuable by the very actor being gated, so it is not used — ADR 0010).
#
# FORMAT — one armed action per line, three pipe-separated fields:
#
#   <action-key> | <memory-slug-or-path> | <note>
#
#   <action-key>        MUST be one of the plugin's CLOSED, reviewed enum keys (below). You
#                       pick a key from the enum — you do NOT write a match pattern. The
#                       matcher is shared plugin code (hooks/lib/action-gate.sh): it tokenizes
#                       the command (strips FOO=bar env-prefixes, accepts path-prefixed bins
#                       and npx / bash -c wrappers, walks compound segments) and maps it to a
#                       key. Per-line user regex is deliberately NOT supported — it would
#                       re-import the unreviewed greedy-match / string-proxy bug class.
#   <memory-slug-or-path>  the memory entry holding the fix, e.g. feedback_deploy_author_fix
#                          (or docs/bootstrap/incidents/2026-06-20-deploy-author/README.md). Injected
#                          verbatim as a pointer; the hook does not read the file for you.
#   <note>              a one-line reminder of the actual fix, surfaced inline with the slug.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored. Surrounding whitespace is trimmed.
#
# CLOSED ACTION-KEY ENUM (the only keys the matcher can ever produce — see
# hooks/lib/action-gate.sh ACTION_KEY_ENUM). Arming a key NOT in this list is an ORPHAN:
# the memo can never fire, and scripts/doctor.sh reports it (surfaced, never blocked). Need a
# new action covered? That is a reviewed plugin-level enum change (add the key + a matcher
# arm in action-gate.sh + a test), not a new pattern in this file.
#
#   prod-deploy       a production deploy (e.g. `vercel deploy --prod`, incl. `--production`)
#                     SPECIAL (ADR 0014): this key ALSO carries a plugin-owned universal doctrine
#                     ("before claiming done — verbatim-cross-check each clause; for a reinterpreted
#                     spec confirm via an output mock, not a scope menu; a misshipped prod deploy is
#                     an incident, not completion") that fires even if you do NOT arm it here. Arm it
#                     only to ADD a project-specific memo, appended after the universal one.
#   prod-db-migrate   a production DB migration apply (e.g. `prisma migrate deploy`)
#   data-backfill     rewriting existing data (backfill/data-migrate script, `prisma db execute`,
#                     a sql-client inline UPDATE/DELETE, or a knex/sequelize/typeorm/alembic run).
#                     SPECIAL (ADR 0013): this key ALSO carries a plugin-owned universal doctrine
#                     ("repair vs spec — is the missingness systematic? the oracle is the domain
#                     owner, not the data") that fires even if you do NOT arm it here. Arm it only
#                     to ADD a project-specific memo, appended after the universal one.
#
# EXAMPLES (delete and replace with your own armed actions):

prod-deploy     | feedback_deploy_author_fix | always pass --build-env DEPLOY_AUTHOR=ci before --prod
prod-db-migrate | feedback_migrate_window    | run only inside the maintenance window; take a snapshot first
# data-backfill | project_demo_lane_service_null_is_spec | demo提案レーンは service null が仕様 — backfillするな
